results.answer:
Fixed. The change:

```js
// Before
return net + net * rate;

// After  
const total = net + net * rate;
return Math.round(total * 100) / 100;
```

The problem was standard IEEE 754 floating-point imprecision (`9.1 * 1.1` produces `10.010000000000002`). Rounding the final result to 2 decimal places with `Math.round(total * 100) / 100` gives exact cent-level precision. All 2 tests pass.

